\section{Committee structure and activities}

The ECFA ECR Committee was established in 2020 to voice the concerns and needs of young researchers within the ECFA community. As revealed in the ECFA survey, young researchers face several challenges, including stable careers, remote work, networking, and access to leadership opportunities. To address these issues, the ECFA ECR Committee launched several activities, described below.

\section{Workshops}

The ECFA ECR Committee organized two online workshops on Career Development and Mental Health in February 2022, bringing together 67 young researchers and established experts. The workshop on Career Development explored innovative approaches to job security, remote work, and time management, while the Mental Health workshop highlighted the significance of self-care and provided access to mental health resources. Future workshops are planned on Networking and Leadership.

\section{Online community}

The ECFA ECR Committee launched a private Discord channel for young researchers to share their experiences, ask for advice, and engage in discussions on various topics. As a result, the community has grown, and members now participate in surveys, share news and events, and collaborate on activities.

